  {
    "statement": "Using textured surfaces of 1 mm or less had mixed effects on non-mobile invertebrate abundance, depending on the site.",
    "citations": [
      "3449"
    ]
  },
  {
    "statement": "Creating physical habitat complexity through holes, pits, grooves, flexible habitats, and transplanting organisms provides the most reliable interventions for increasing invertebrate abundance on subtidal artificial structures.",
